• store_type is passed directly to Java:

  KeyStore.getInstance(store_type)

  So valid values depend on the JDK/security providers available at runtime.

  On this local Java 17 environment, supported KeyStore types are:

  CaseExactJKS
  DKS
  JCEKS
  JKS
  PKCS12

  For JKSKeyInlineBase64Provider with an AES secret key, the practical choices are:

  store_type: "JCEKS"

  or:

  store_type: "PKCS12"

  Use JCEKS if you want the traditional Cassandra TDE secret-key keystore format. Use PKCS12 if you want the modern standard Java keystore format.

  I would avoid JKS for new AES secret-key configs unless you have tested it on every target JDK. DKS and CaseExactJKS are special-purpose and not a good default here.


• set -e
  umask 077
  STORE=/tmp/cassandra-tde-aes256.p12
  rm -f "$STORE"

  keytool -genseckey \
    -alias cassandra_tde_key \
    -keyalg AES \
    -keysize 256 \
    -storetype PKCS12 \
    -keystore "$STORE" \
    -storepass 'changeit-store-password' \
    -keypass 'changeit-store-password'

  base64 -w 0 "$STORE"

  Note: for PKCS12, Java typically expects the key password to be the same as the keystore password. In Cassandra config, you can omit key_password or set it equal to keystore_password.

• Yes. A JCEKS or PKCS12 keystore can contain multiple AES secret keys, each under a different alias.

  Example:

  STORE=/tmp/cassandra-tde-keys.jceks
  STOREPASS='changeit-store-password'

  keytool -genseckey \
    -alias key_v1 \
    -keyalg AES \
    -keysize 256 \
    -storetype JCEKS \
    -keystore "$STORE" \
    -storepass "$STOREPASS" \
    -keypass 'key-v1-password'

  keytool -genseckey \
    -alias key_v2 \
    -keyalg AES \
    -keysize 256 \
    -storetype JCEKS \
    -keystore "$STORE" \
    -storepass "$STOREPASS" \
    -keypass 'key-v2-password'

  base64 -w 0 "$STORE"

  Cassandra selects one key by key_alias:

  key_alias: key_v1

  If different entries have different key passwords, set key_password to the password for the alias Cassandra should load. For simpler operation, use the same password for all keys and the keystore.